      "answer": "Asia occupies both regional extremes: it has the greatest maximum Height among Asia, North America, and Europe, while its minimum Height is the lowest of the three regions. [G62] [G64] The regional minimum Heights are 461.0 m for Landmark 81 in Asia, 462.0 m for Lakhta Center in Europe, and 472.0 m for Central Park Tower in North America. [G2] Within Asia, *Burj Khalifa* is an outlier at 828.0 m, with a substantial vertical gap above the other observed Asian buildings. [G23] [G87] North America’s observed composition contains two buildings: Central Park Tower at 472.0 m and One World Trade Center at 541.0 m. [G17] One World Trade Center is the observed North American maximum at 541.0 m. [G30]",
